  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="0198-9260-6b1b-dd9b" name="Syrian and Caananite (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #119 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The city states of Syria and Canaan held valuable economic resources and so both Egypt and the Hittite Empire wished to control them to the exclusion of the other. In addition to forming a battleground for the two regional superpowers, the states were victims of aggression by the Habiru (Israelites) and the Sea Peoples. Allies And Mercenaries: The army may take allies from either the New Kingdom Egyptian or Hittite lists, but not both, representing support from the great powers for a client kingdom.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Syrian and Caananite]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariots and Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariots and Cavalry: up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
